# ThinkLot — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development, or set these in your host's dashboard
# for a deployment. `.env.local` is gitignored; this file is committed.
#
# Exactly ONE variable is required. Everything else lives on the Convex
# deployment, not in the app.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your Convex deployment URL. `npx convex dev` writes this into .env.local for
# you; `npx convex env list` shows it for any deployment.
#
# Without it the app does not crash - it renders a blank page with a
# TypeError in the console, because every page subscribes to Convex. If you see
# a blank screen, check this first. /healthz reports it explicitly.
#
#   dev:        https://<deployment>.convex.cloud
#   production: https://<deployment>.convex.cloud
PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT needed here — set these on the CONVEX deployment instead
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Convex Auth requires these as Convex env vars (npx convex env set NAME value).
# They are listed here so nobody wastes time putting them in this file.
#
#   JWT_PRIVATE_KEY      the PEM private key Convex Auth signs tokens with
#   JWKS                 the matching public key set, as JSON
#   SITE_URL             the deployed origin, for OAuth/magic-link callbacks
#
# Generate the keypair with:
#   npx @convex-dev/auth@latest test
# or follow https://docs.convex.dev/auth
